(D5 - RESOLVED, re-recorded 2026-08-22 against vox 0.4.9. Discrepancy 5
 used to be: the --shared thing-crossing diagnostics located their caret
 by scanning the SOURCE TEXT for the exported function's name and taking
 successive occurrences of it, rather than by the definition's own
 position, so a comment mentioning the name earlier stole the first
 error's caret. On 0.4.9 both errors correctly point at the definition
 (line 24), and both messages now name the function and the crossing
 field/parameter. This header deliberately does not spell the function
 name in prose, a habit worth keeping even though the bug it guarded
 against is fixed.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox shared/D5.vox --shared -o libd5.so
 expected output:
   error: Exported function 'nudged east' takes a point ('start'), which a library interface cannot describe yet
   ...
   error: Exported function 'nudged east' returns a point, which a library interface cannot describe yet
   ...
   Both carets land on D5.vox:24:5, the definition. No library is produced; this is a compile error.
)
Library geometrykit version "1.0".

(A comment that mentions 'nudged east'.)

A thing called point has
  a number called x is 0.

To 'nudged east' with a point called start.
  Return a point, start.
